00\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015MINUTES OF A REGULAR MEETING OF\rTHE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF CALABASAS,\rCALIFORNIA, HELD WEDNESDAY, OCTOBER 14, 2009\r\rMayor Wolfson called the meeting to order at 7:04 p.m. in the City Council Chambers, 100 Civic Center Way, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Wolfson, Mayor pro Tem Groveman, Councilmembers Bozajian, Maurer and Washburn.\r Absent: None.\r Staff: Cohen, Colantuono, Coroalles, Farassati, Peirce, Rubin, Tamuri, Yalda.\r \r The Pledge of Allegiance was led by Karyn Foley. \r\rAPPROVAL OF AGENDA\r \r Councilmember Washburn moved, seconded by Councilmember Maurer, to approve the agenda. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\rANNOUNCEMENTS/INTRODUCTIONS\r\r Councilmember Washburn announced that the Calabasas Pumpkin Festival will be taking place October 17 � 18. Councilmember Bozajian announced the upcoming event at the Civic Center on October 25, �Ghost Stories by the Campfire.� Councilmember Maurer spoke regarding an upcoming blood drive at Lupin Hill Elementary and an Artists Reception event at the Calabasas Library. Mayor Wolfson spoke regarding the Great California Shake Out earthquake drill happening on October 15 and he announced two upcoming flu clinics that will be occurring in the City.\r\rORAL COMMUNICATIONS - PUBLIC COMMENT:\r\r Karyn Foley, Calabasas, spoke regarding the upcoming Artists Reception featuring Michael Newman. David Litt, Calabasas, spoke regarding issues with the Landscape Maintenance Districts in the Calabasas Park Homeowners Association.\r\rCONSENT ITEMS \r\r Approval of meeting minutes from September 23, 2009.\r\r3. Recommendation from the Parks, Recreation and Education Commission to award Community Service Grants for the First Funding Cycle of FY 09/10. \r\r4. Approve budget for Las Virgenes Creek Restoration Project�Phase 2 in the amount of $85,000.00. \r\rApproval of City budget adjustment and expenditure of Supplemental Law Enforcement Services Fund for Fiscal Year 2009/2010. \r\r Recommendation to accept completion for the Juan Bautista de Anza Park Trellis/Patio Project Specification No. 08-09-05 by Malibu Pacific Tennis Courts Inc, and to direct the City Clerk to file notice of completion. \r\r Authorization to modify Fiscal Year 2009-10 budget for Landscape Maintenance District 22. \r\rCouncilmember Washburn moved, seconded by Councilmember Maurer, to approve Consent Items 1, 3, 4, 5, 6 and 7 with Councilmember Maurer�s ABSTENTION on Item #1. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\r The following item was heard out of order of the agenda:\r Adoption of Ordinance No. 2009-264, amending Title 15 of the Calabasas Municipal Code Section K 13 (b) (3) (a) of the On Site Waste Water Treatment System Operating Permit Program to mandate initial inspections within a six month period.\r\rMichael Karagosian, Calabasas, Russ Sutherland, Topanga, Jody Thomas, Topanga, Gail Newman, Calabasas, Babette Gibbs, Topanga, Jack Trompeter, Calabasas, spoke in opposition to the proposed ordinance in Item #2, specifically the shortened time frame for septic system inspections from two years to six months.\r\rFollowing discussion, Mayor Wolfson moved, seconded by Mayor pro Tem Groveman, to waive further reading and re-introduce Ordinance No. 2009-264 with the amendment to the On Site Waste Water Treatment System Operating Permit Program to allow for a five month extension after the initial six month period has passed. MOTION CARRIED 3/2. Councilmember Maurer and Councilmember Bozajian voted NO.\r\rUNFINISHED BUSINESS \r\r8. Adoption of Resolution No. 2009-1208, establishing an Onsite Waste Water Treatment System (OWTS) Inspection grant program in the amount of $25,000. \r\r Councilmember Washburn moved, seconded by Mayor pro Tem Groveman, to adopt Resolution No. 2009-1208, establishing an Onsite Waste Water Treatment System (OWTS) Inspection grant program in the amount of $25,000 with revisions to the Guidelines to remove the term �residency� and replace with �property ownership.� MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rNEW BUSINESS \r\rUpdates on local efforts and State legislation to ban the use of plastic grocery bags.\r\rAlex Farassati, Environmental Services Manager, presented the staff report.\r\rThere was no action taken.\r\rIntroduction of Ordinance No. 2009-266, amending Chapter 8.16 of Title 8 of the Calabasas Municipal Code relating to unauthorized refuse containers. \r\rDaniel Pankau, Environmental Services Assistant, presented the staff report.\r\rChuck Jelloian, Chatsworth, spoke in support of the proposed ordinance and is requesting the addition that the franchisee to impound the unauthorized bins.\r\r Councilmember Washburn moved, seconded by Councilmember Bozajian, to waive further reading and introduce Ordinance No. 2009-266, amending Chapter 8.16 of Title 8 of the Calabasas Municipal Code relating to unauthorized refuse containers. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rDiscussion of a City financing program to encourage installation of private energy systems in Calabasas.\r\rMaureen Tamuri, Community Development Director, provided the staff report.\r\rRichard Blackledge, spoke in support of implementing a City financing program to encourage installation of private energy systems in Calabasas.\r\rThe City Council concurred to direct staff to move forward with a City financing program.\r\rINFORMATIONAL REPORTS\r\rCheck Register for the period of September 16, 2009 to September 30, 2009. \r\rThere was no action taken.\rTASK FORCE REPORTS \r\r There were no task force reports.\r\rCITY MANAGER�S REPORT \r\r Robert Yalda, City Engineer, and City Manager Coroalles presented an update on the Lost Hills Interchange Project.\r\rFUTURE AGENDA ITEMS \r\r The City Council requested that an item regarding instituting ethics standards and procedures for Commissioners and an item regarding citizens serving on the civil grand jury be placed on a future agenda.\r\r\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015ADJOURN\r\rThe City Council adjourned at 9:35 P.M. to their next regular meeting, which will be held on Wednesday, October 28, 2009 at 7:00 P.M. \r\r\r\r\r\r__________________________________\rGwen Peirce, CMC, City Clerk\r\r\r\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0013 PAGE \\* MERGEFORMAT \u00142\u0015\r\r\r\u0013 PAGE \\* MERGEFORMAT \u00143\u0015\r10/14/09\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u00